@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium BPMN choreography — 6-8 tasks, gateway, message variables.
'   usecase:      Price negotiation between Buyer and Seller with a counter-offer loop.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       business-process
' ============================================================================
title Example BPMN Choreography - Negotiation

' Choreography: no pools. Each task is banded by participants.
' Initiator band = white; responder band = shaded.
' Message variables (e.g. QuoteId, Price) flow between tasks and
' can be referenced by gateway conditions.

' --- Events ---------------------------------------------------------------
usecase " " as Start
usecase " " as EndAccept
usecase " " as EndReject

' --- Tasks (banded) -------------------------------------------------------
package "Request Quote\n[ Buyer | Seller ]" as T1
package "Send Quote\n[ Seller | Buyer ]" as T2
package "Counter Offer\n[ Buyer | Seller ]" as T3
package "Evaluate Offer\n[ Seller | Buyer ]" as T4
package "Accept Quote\n[ Buyer | Seller ]" as T5
package "Issue PO\n[ Buyer | Seller ]" as T6

' --- Gateway --------------------------------------------------------------
usecase "Acceptable?" as X1

Start --> T1
T1 --> T2
T2 --> X1
X1 --> T5 : (buyer accepts)
X1 --> T3 : (buyer counters)
T3 --> T4
T4 --> X1 : re-evaluate
' Buyer's accept path
T5 --> T6
T6 --> EndAccept
' Hard fail after N rounds would route here
T4 --> EndReject : (seller rejects)

note top of T1
  <b>Message variables</b>
  T1 establishes QuoteId; later
  tasks reference it. Price
  variable is updated by T2/T3.
end note

note right of X1
  <b>Gateway on message data</b>
  Branch condition reads a
  variable (e.g. Price <= Budget).
end note

note bottom of T4
  <b>Role swap</b>
  Seller initiates the evaluation
  message; Buyer responds with
  acceptance or new counter.
end note

@enduml
